From 5c4fc82f8e80f6b7c1989f52a8db91863ba86c9f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: well0nez <well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 20:16:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 41/77] sunxi: h713: a device tree named after the board that
 boots it

Every HY310 build so far has loaded "sun50i-h713-hy200-qz713df-a1", the
bench board's tree. That is not a mistake in the electrical sense -- the
two boards differ in the DRAM clock, which lives in the defconfig, and in
the panel, which no node describes because the display coprocessor drives
it from its own tables -- but it is one in every other sense. A boot log
that names another board tells the reader this is a board nobody has built
for, and the next person to add a third board has no example of how to.

So: a tree of its own, as an include of the bench board's plus model and
compatible. Nothing is copied, so nothing can drift. What we patched into
the HY200 tree stays there for now; moving the board-specific parts out is
a later cleanup, not this change.

No Makefile entry goes with it. This tree builds device trees through
scripts/Makefile.dts, which derives dtb-y from CONFIG_DEFAULT_DEVICE_TREE,
CONFIG_OF_LIST and CONFIG_SPL_OF_LIST -- the per-vendor lists of the Linux
tree do not exist here. Naming the tree in the defconfig is the whole
wiring, and CONFIG_OF_LIST follows it by default.

Checked by compiling both trees and comparing them: the HY310 dtb differs
from the HY200 dtb in model and compatible and in nothing else.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../src/arm64/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy310.dts | 24 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 dts/upstream/src/arm64/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy310.dts

diff --git a/dts/upstream/src/arm64/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy310.dts b/dts/upstream/src/arm64/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy310.dts
new file mode 100644
index 00000000000..b8270762d98
--- /dev/null
+++ b/dts/upstream/src/arm64/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy310.dts
@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: (GPL-2.0+ OR MIT)
+/*
+ * MagCubic HY310 projector, board silkscreen HY260_QZ713_V3.1.
+ *
+ * Electrically this is the bench board's device tree: DDR3, the same pin
+ * assignments, the same peripherals. What differs is the DRAM clock (792 MHz
+ * instead of 624, and that lives in the defconfig, not here) and the panel,
+ * which no node in this tree describes because the panel is driven by the
+ * display coprocessor's own tables.
+ *
+ * So the tree is an include, not a copy. The reason it exists at all is that
+ * a board should boot a device tree named after itself: until now the HY310
+ * shipped "sun50i-h713-hy200-qz713df-a1", which tells anyone reading a boot
+ * log that this is a board nobody has built for. Anything genuinely
+ * board-specific that we patched into the HY200 tree stays there for now;
+ * moving it out is a later cleanup, not this change.
+ */
+
+#include "sun50i-h713-hy200-qz713df-a1.dts"
+
+/ {
+	model = "MagCubic HY310 (HY260_QZ713_V3.1)";
+	compatible = "magcubic,hy310", "allwinner,sun50i-h713";
+};
